  "provenance": "M46/ADR-037 Decision 5. The third schema twin: an escalate run carries exactly one field the other two modes do not (`legs`), the TraceStep is untouched \u2014 ADR-028 \u00a77's 'the trace gains no fields' survives a policy that concatenates two runs' traces, because the concatenation uses `i` and `superseded_by` as they already are \u2014 and `legs_entry` pins the new sub-shape, so a leg record that quietly stopped reporting its own budgets or its superseded extractions is red here. The plan leg is scripted to fail so that a two-leg run is what gets graded: a one-leg escalate run would leave every claim about the second entry unmade."
